<title>NORWAY: Aker Maritime wins NOK 180 mln drill deal.</title>
<headline>Aker Maritime wins NOK 180 mln drill deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aker Maritime ASA said on Tuesday its Maritime Hydraulics unit had won a contract to deliver a 180 million crown RamRig drilling package to drilling contractor Dolphin.</p>
<p>Dolphin's rig Borgland Dolphin is to be converted into a drilling platform for use under a long-term agreement with state Norwegian oil company Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil).</p>
<p>Maritime Hydraulics will deliver the RamRig unit and associated equipment in May 1998.</p>
<p>Under a separate contract, Aker Engineering, will be responsible for pre-engineering of the Borgland Dolphin conversion.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
